<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: RUGBY UNION-FRANCE BEAT IRELAND 32-15.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-FRANCE BEAT IRELAND 32-15.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>France beat Ireland 32-15 (halftime 12-12) in their opening Five Nations rugby union match on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Ireland - Penalties: Eric Elwood (5)</p>
<p>France - Tries: David Venditti (3), Fabien Galthie. Conversions: Thomas Castaignede (3). Penalties: Thomas Castaignede (2).</p>
